##### Handling Offline Scenarios

**Before Going Offline:**
- Sync all assigned tasks to local storage
- Pre-download maps for job sites (external app)
- Ensure device has sufficient storage

**While Offline:**
- Continue working normally — all data is cached
- Take photos (compressed automatically for storage efficiency)
- Update task statuses and notes
- Monitor offline data size indicator

**After Reconnecting:**
- Click "Sync Now" or wait for automatic sync
- Verify all pending items upload successfully
- Check for any sync conflicts (rare)

#### Image Compression

To conserve bandwidth and device storage, the Field App automatically compresses photos before upload:

- **Compression Algorithm** — Optimized for quality vs. file size
- **Target Size** — ~500KB per photo (adjustable)
- **Original Quality** — Retained for critical documentation photos
- **Batch Upload** — Compresses and uploads photos during sync

> **Tip:** Photos taken while offline are compressed and queued for upload. When connection is restored, they upload automatically in the background.

#### GPS Tracking

The Field App leverages device GPS for location-based features:

**Features:**
- **Real-time Position** — Track technician movement throughout the day
- **Geofencing** — Automatic check-in when arriving at job site
- **Route Optimization** — Suggest efficient travel routes between tasks
- **Location Verification** — Confirm work was performed at correct address

**Accuracy Indicators:**
- **High Accuracy** (< 10m) — 🟢 Green indicator
- **Medium Accuracy** (10-50m) — 🟡 Yellow indicator
- **Low Accuracy** (> 50m) — 🔴 Red indicator

> **Important:** GPS accuracy depends on device quality, satellite visibility, and environmental factors (buildings, trees, weather). Indoor locations may have reduced accuracy.

#### Sync Behavior

The Field App uses intelligent sync logic to minimize data usage and maximize reliability:

**Automatic Sync Triggers:**
- Every 5 minutes when online (configurable)
- When app is opened or brought to foreground
- After completing a task
- When network connection is restored

**Manual Sync:**
- Click "Sync Now" button in Offline Status card
- Useful before going offline or when urgent updates are needed

**Sync Priority Order:**
1. Task status updates (highest priority)
2. Form data and notes
3. Compressed photos (lowest priority, largest data)

**Conflict Resolution:**
- Server data takes precedence by default
- User is notified if manual resolution is required
- Conflicts are rare — typically occur if same task is edited on multiple devices simultaneously

