**Creating New Tasks:**
Click **+ New Task** button to open task creation modal:

**Required Fields:**
- `title` — Task summary (max 100 characters)
- `assigned_to` — Select agent from dropdown
- `priority` — Low, Normal, High, Urgent

**Optional Fields:**
- `description` — Detailed task instructions
- `tags` — Comma-separated labels for organization
- `parent_id` — Link to parent task (for subtasks)

**Task Priority Guidelines:**
- **Urgent** — Critical issues requiring immediate attention (e.g., production outage)
- **High** — Important tasks needed soon (e.g., deployment, security fix)
- **Normal** — Standard tasks for routine work
- **Low** — Nice-to-have improvements, documentation updates

#### Workflows

##### Monitoring Agent Health

**Daily Check:**
1. Open Mission Control Dashboard tab
2. Verify all agents show "Online" status (green badges)
3. Check system health metrics (memory, disk, load average)
4. Review service status — all should be ✅ Active
5. If any agent is Offline:
   - Check last heartbeat timestamp
   - Review last message in Live Feed
   - Contact system administrator if offline >30 minutes

##### Creating and Assigning Tasks

**Scenario:** Deploy urgent security patch

1. Navigate to **Task Board** tab
2. Click **+ New Task** button
3. Fill in task details:
   - Title: "Deploy security patch for authentication module"
   - Description: "Apply patch from security@velocityfibre.co.za email. Test staging first."
   - Assigned to: **Forge** (deployment specialist)
   - Priority: **Urgent**
   - Tags: "security, deployment, urgent"
4. Click **Create Task**
5. Task appears in "Pending" column
6. Forge automatically picks up urgent tasks within 1-2 minutes
7. Task moves to "In Progress" when Forge starts work
8. Monitor Live Feed for Forge status updates
9. Task moves to "Completed" when Forge finishes
10. Review Forge's completion message for results

##### Reviewing Agent Communications

**Use Case:** Understand what agents accomplished today

1. Open **Live Feed** tab
2. Set time filter to "Today"
3. Filter by message type: **Report**
4. Review completion messages from each agent
5. Note any alerts or errors
6. Check if any agents requested assistance
7. Follow up on any blocked or incomplete tasks

##### Troubleshooting Agent Issues

**Symptom:** Agent stuck on task for >30 minutes

**Steps:**
1. Check **Dashboard** → Find agent status card
2. Review current task and time elapsed
3. Open **Live Feed** → Filter by agent name
4. Look for error messages or "blocked" status
5. Check **Task Board** → View task details
6. Options:
   - **Wait** — If task is complex, allow more time
   - **Reassign** — Move task to different agent if possible
   - **Delete & Recreate** — If task is stuck, cancel and retry
   - **Contact Admin** — For persistent issues

#### Permissions

Access to Mission Control is restricted to administrative roles:

| Permission | Description | Typical Roles |
|------------|-------------|---------------|
| `communications.mission-control.view` | View Mission Control dashboard | Managers, Supervisors |
| `communications.mission-control.manage-tasks` | Create and assign tasks | Managers, Administrators |
| `communications.mission-control.admin` | Full control including agent logs | System Administrators |

> **Note:** Contact your system administrator to request Mission Control access.

#### Best Practices

**For Supervisors:**
- Check Mission Control at start of day to verify all agents are online
- Monitor pending tasks to ensure work is being picked up
- Review completed tasks to understand agent productivity
- Use Live Feed to track progress on critical tasks
- Create tasks with clear, specific instructions

**For Administrators:**
- Set up alerts for agent offline status (>15 minutes)
- Monitor system health metrics regularly
- Review agent logs weekly for errors or patterns
- Keep task backlog under 20 pending tasks
- Archive completed tasks older than 30 days

**For Task Creation:**
- Use descriptive titles (good: "Deploy v2.3.1 to production", bad: "Deploy stuff")
- Include context in description field
- Tag tasks for easy filtering (e.g., "deployment", "urgent", "documentation")
- Assign to correct specialist agent for the work type
- Set realistic priorities (not everything is Urgent)

#### Understanding Agent Coordination

**How Agents Pick Up Tasks:**
1. Agents poll Mission Control every 15 minutes
2. Each agent checks for tasks assigned to them
3. Tasks are prioritized: Urgent → High → Normal → Low
4. Agents work on one task at a time (serial processing)
5. Upon completion, agents mark task "Completed" and pick up next task

**Agent Collaboration:**
Agents can communicate and coordinate:
- **Forge** deploys code → **Sentinel** monitors logs → **Pixel** runs UI audit → **Scribe** updates docs
- **Velo** creates deployment task → **Forge** executes → **Velo** notifies user via WhatsApp
- **Sentinel** detects error → creates task for **Forge** to investigate

**Cross-Agent Tasks:**
Some tasks require multiple agents:
- Tag with multiple agent names: "forge,sentinel"
- Create parent task with subtasks for each agent
- Use Live Feed to coordinate handoffs

#### System Architecture

**Mission Control Backend:**
- **API Endpoint:** `/api/mission-control/dashboard`
- **Database:** PostgreSQL tables (agents, messages, tasks)
- **Polling Frequency:** Agents check every 15 minutes
- **Message Retention:** 30 days (configurable)
- **Task Retention:** 90 days (completed), indefinite (pending/in-progress)

**Agent Heartbeat:**
Agents send heartbeat every 5 minutes:
- Updates `last_heartbeat` timestamp
- Updates `status` (online/busy/offline)
- Reports current task (if any)
- Sends system metrics (memory, CPU, errors)

**Data Refresh:**
- Dashboard data refreshes every 30 seconds (automatic)
- Manual refresh available via **Refresh** button
- Live Feed updates every 10 seconds
- Task Board updates on any task change (WebSocket)

#### Troubleshooting

**Common Issues:**

| Issue | Cause | Solution |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Agent shows "Offline" | No heartbeat in >15 minutes | Check agent logs, restart agent service |
| Task stuck in "Pending" | No agent assigned or agent offline | Reassign to different agent or wait for agent to come online |
| Live Feed not updating | Browser connection issue | Click Refresh button, check internet connection |
| Can't create tasks | Missing permissions | Request `manage-tasks` permission from admin |
| Statistics seem wrong | Cache or timing issue | Click Refresh, wait 30 seconds for cache to clear |

**Performance Issues:**
- If dashboard loads slowly, archive old completed tasks
- If Live Feed lags, reduce retention period (default 30 days)
- If task board is cluttered, filter by status or agent

**Support:**
- For agent issues: Check Sentinel logs first
- For task problems: Review task description and agent capabilities
- For access issues: Contact system administrator
- For bugs: Email support@velocityfibre.co.za with screenshot

#### Integration with Other Systems

Mission Control integrates with:

- **WhatsApp (Section 12.2)** — Velo agent sends task updates via WhatsApp
- **Help Center (Section 12.4)** — Scribe agent maintains documentation
- **QField Sync (Section 13.2)** — Field operations coordination
- **Analytics (Section 11)** — Agent activity metrics included in reports

**API Integration:**
External systems can interact with Mission Control:

```bash
# Create a task via API
POST /api/mission-control/tasks
{
  "title": "Deploy to production",
  "assigned_to": "Forge",
  "priority": "high"
}

# Get agent status
GET /api/mission-control/agents

# View live feed messages
GET /api/mission-control/messages?limit=50
```

> **Note:** API requires authentication token. Contact administrator for API access.

