### Appendix F: Troubleshooting Guide

#### General Issues

| Problem | Solution |
|---------|----------|
| **Page not loading** | Refresh the page. Check your internet connection. Try clearing browser cache. |
| **"Unauthorized" error** | Your session may have expired. Log out and log back in. |
| **Missing menu items** | Your role may not have access. Contact your administrator. |
| **Data not updating** | Try refreshing the page. Some data syncs on intervals (e.g., QContact). |
| **Slow performance** | Check your internet speed. Try a different browser. Close unnecessary tabs. |
| **Dark mode issues** | Toggle theme in header menu. Some components show white backgrounds in dark mode (see Appendix G). Use light mode for consistent experience. |

#### Module-Specific Issues

| Module | Problem | Solution |
|--------|---------|----------|
| **Activate** | Photos not loading | Check if the 1Map API is responding. Photos require VPS connectivity. |
| **Activate** | VLM categorization wrong | Correct the categorization manually — corrections improve future accuracy. |
| **Activate** | PP Data not importing | Ensure OES Excel file has "PP DATA" sheet with correct format. |
| **Field Operations** | QField QA photos missing | Check MinIO connectivity and photo path format with version suffixes. |
| **Field Operations** | AI validation stuck | Check VLM service at port 8100. Verify logger format in API calls. |
| **NOC** | QContact sync failed | Check Data Sync tab for error details. Try manual sync. |
| **NOC** | Cannot move ticket status | Check required fields (fault cause, verification). Verify RBAC permissions. |
| **Procurement** | BOQ import fails | Ensure Excel has headers in row 1. Check column mapper for correct mappings. |
| **Procurement** | PO stuck in approval | Check Approvals tab. The assigned approver may need to take action. |
| **Fleet** | Plate scan not recognized | Ensure good lighting and clear plate photo. Enter plate manually if needed. |
| **Fleet** | Check-in not visible to manager | Ensure user has manager role. Check RBAC permissions. |
| **Assets** | Cannot delete asset | Assets must be checked in (status: Available) before deletion. |
| **HR** | Import errors | Check CSV formatting. Required fields: first_name, last_name, email. |
| **HR** | Missing staff tabs | Check granular permissions. User may not have access to specific tabs. |
| **Communications** | Meetings not showing | Check participant access. Users only see meetings they attended. |
| **Communications** | AI Chat not responding | Refresh page. Check internet connection. AI Chat requires active connection. |
| **Communications** | Help Center search not working | Try different keywords. Use topic filter. Some content may be recently added. |
| **System** | Data Sync tabs missing | Check granular permissions. Loading spinner indicates permission check. |

### Appendix G: Accessibility & WCAG Compliance

#### Overview

FibreFlow is committed to making the application accessible to all users, regardless of ability or assistive technology used. This section documents the current accessibility status, known limitations, and recommended best practices.

> **Important:** This section reflects audit findings as of February 2026. Accessibility improvements are ongoing, and this documentation will be updated as enhancements are implemented.

#### Current Accessibility Status

**WCAG 2.1 Compliance Level:** Partial (Level AA targeted)

FibreFlow has undergone accessibility audits for Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.1 compliance. The following table summarizes the current status:

| WCAG Principle | Compliance Level | Status |
|----------------|------------------|--------|
| **Perceivable** | Partial | Some contrast issues in dark mode; images have alt text |
| **Operable** | Good | Keyboard navigation supported; no keyboard traps |
| **Understandable** | Good | Clear labeling; consistent navigation patterns |
| **Robust** | Good | Valid HTML; ARIA landmarks in use |

#### Known Accessibility Issues **(As of February 2026)**

Based on comprehensive UI/UX audits conducted in February 2026, the following accessibility issues have been identified:

##### Critical Issues (WCAG Level A Failures)

1. **Insufficient Color Contrast (WCAG 1.4.3)**
   - **Impact:** Some text elements do not meet the minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio required for normal text
   - **Affected Areas:** Login page, certain dashboard cards, some button states
   - **Status:** Under review
   - **Workaround:** Use dark mode for improved contrast on most pages

2. **Missing Form Labels (WCAG 1.3.1, 4.1.2)**
   - **Impact:** Some form inputs lack proper labels, making them difficult for screen reader users
   - **Affected Areas:** Certain modal forms and inline edit fields
   - **Status:** Under review
   - **Workaround:** Contact support for assistance with form completion

3. **Keyboard Focus Indicators (WCAG 2.4.7)**
   - **Impact:** Some interactive elements lack visible focus indicators when navigating with keyboard
   - **Affected Areas:** Certain dropdown menus and custom controls
   - **Status:** Under review
   - **Workaround:** Use mouse/touch navigation for affected elements

##### Moderate Issues (WCAG Level AA)

1. **Dark Mode Inconsistencies**
   - **Impact:** Some components display white or light-colored backgrounds in dark mode
   - **Scope:** 20+ identified components across the application
   - **Affected Components:** Certain modals, dropdown menus, data tables, and cards
   - **Status:** Comprehensive fix in progress
   - **Workaround:** Use light mode for consistent visual experience

2. **Hardcoded Colors**
   - **Impact:** Theme customization is limited; some colors do not adapt to user preferences
   - **Scope:** 273 instances of hardcoded color values identified
   - **Status:** Systematic refactoring planned
   - **Workaround:** None currently available

3. **Touch Target Sizes (WCAG 2.5.5)**
   - **Impact:** Some interactive elements are smaller than recommended 44x44 pixel minimum
   - **Affected Areas:** Certain icon buttons, close buttons on modals
   - **Status:** Under review
   - **Workaround:** Use desktop browser with mouse for better control

#### Accessibility Features Currently Available

Despite the known issues, FibreFlow includes several accessibility features:

✅ **Keyboard Navigation**
- Most pages support full keyboard navigation using Tab, Shift+Tab, Enter, and Escape
- Modal dialogs can be closed with Escape key
- Forms support Ctrl+Enter for submission
- See Appendix C for full keyboard shortcut list

✅ **Screen Reader Support**
- Semantic HTML structure with proper heading hierarchy
- ARIA landmarks for major page regions
- Alt text for informational images
- Form field associations with labels (where implemented)

✅ **Responsive Text**
- Text can be resized up to 200% using browser zoom without loss of functionality
- Font sizes use relative units (rem) for better scaling

✅ **Dark Mode Toggle**
- Available in header menu (user icon → Theme toggle)
- Preference is saved per user session
- See "Dark Mode Usage" section below for details

#### Dark Mode Usage & Known Limitations

##### Enabling Dark Mode

1. Click your **user icon** in the top-right header
2. Click the **moon/sun icon** to toggle between light and dark themes
3. Your preference is saved automatically

##### Dark Mode Support Status **(February 2026)**

> **Important:** Dark mode is currently in a transitional state. While most core components work correctly, some areas have incomplete dark mode support.

**Components with Full Dark Mode Support (Grade A+):**
- ✅ GlassCard component (primary card system)
- ✅ VelocityButton component (all button variants)
- ✅ Main navigation sidebar
- ✅ Header and user menu
- ✅ Dashboard page
- ✅ Most data tables

**Known Dark Mode Issues:**
- ❌ **White backgrounds:** Some modal dialogs, dropdowns, and overlay components may display white backgrounds in dark mode
- ❌ **Text contrast:** Certain text elements may have poor contrast in dark mode
- ❌ **Inconsistent styling:** Some pages may show mixed light/dark elements
- ⚠️ **Browser compatibility:** Older browsers (IE11, Safari <13) may have rendering issues

**Recommendation:**
- If you encounter visual inconsistencies in dark mode, **switch to light mode** for a more consistent experience
- Dark mode improvements are actively being implemented
- Check future version updates (Appendix A) for dark mode enhancements

#### Best Practices for Users with Accessibility Needs

##### For Screen Reader Users

1. **Use landmarks for navigation:** FibreFlow uses ARIA landmarks (main, navigation, complementary) to help you skip between major sections
2. **Check form labels:** If a form field is not announced properly, use the visible label text to identify the field
3. **Modal dialogs:** When modals open, focus should move to the dialog. Press Escape to close
4. **Tables:** Data tables include proper headers; use your screen reader's table navigation mode

**Recommended Screen Readers:**
- NVDA (Windows) - Good support
- JAWS (Windows) - Good support
- VoiceOver (macOS/iOS) - Good support
- TalkBack (Android) - Limited testing; some issues may exist

##### For Keyboard-Only Users

1. **Use Tab/Shift+Tab** to navigate between interactive elements
2. **Press Enter** to activate buttons and links
3. **Press Escape** to close modals and cancel operations
4. **Use arrow keys** within dropdown menus and lists
5. **See Appendix C** for additional keyboard shortcuts

**Known keyboard navigation issues:**
- Some custom dropdowns may not be fully keyboard-accessible
- Certain drag-and-drop interfaces require mouse interaction
- File upload dialogs may require screen reader assistance

##### For Users with Low Vision

1. **Use browser zoom:** Ctrl/Cmd + (+) to zoom in, (-) to zoom out. FibreFlow supports up to 200% zoom
2. **Enable dark mode** for reduced eye strain in low-light environments (see limitations above)
3. **Increase text size:** Use your browser's text-only zoom feature for larger text
4. **Use high contrast mode:** Your operating system's high contrast mode should work with FibreFlow

##### For Users with Color Blindness

> **Important:** FibreFlow currently uses color as the primary indicator for some status information. This may cause difficulties for users with color vision deficiencies.

**Current limitations:**
- Status indicators (green/red/yellow) may be difficult to distinguish
- Chart colors may not be color-blind friendly

**Workarounds:**
- Use browser extensions like "Color Blind Pal" or "High Contrast" mode
- Status information is also conveyed through icons and text labels in most cases
- Contact support for assistance interpreting color-coded information

#### Reporting Accessibility Issues

If you encounter an accessibility barrier not documented here, please report it to your system administrator with:

1. **Description** of the barrier (e.g., "Cannot tab to the Save button")
2. **Location** (module, page, and specific feature)
3. **Assistive technology** you are using (e.g., NVDA screen reader, keyboard only)
4. **Browser and version** (e.g., Chrome 120, Firefox 115)

Your feedback helps improve FibreFlow's accessibility for all users.

#### Future Accessibility Roadmap

**Planned improvements:**
- ✅ Comprehensive dark mode consistency fixes (in progress)
- ✅ WCAG 2.1 Level AA compliance audit completion (in progress)
- 🔄 Fix all critical contrast issues
- 🔄 Implement missing form labels
- 🔄 Add visible focus indicators to all interactive elements
- 🔄 Convert hardcoded colors to theme variables
- 📋 Add customizable color schemes for color-blind users
- 📋 Implement adjustable text sizing controls
- 📋 Third-party WCAG audit and certification

**Legend:** ✅ In progress | 🔄 Planned (Q1 2026) | 📋 Planned (Q2 2026+)

